Hi,

	thanks.


	I now have been able to replicate the build errors on win 64.  I'll let you know what I find out.


	If anyone is curious, to build R-2.11 on 64 bit on windows, you have to
	1. Install Rtools from  http://www.murdoch-sutherland.com/Rtools/Rtools211.exe ( see http://www.murdoch-sutherland.com/Rtools )
	2. Unpack (http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools/oldWin64toolchain.zip ) in your Rtools home ( see http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools )
	3. configure your PATH to find the oldWin64\bin befor the Rtools\MinGW\bin
	3. Unpack R-2.11.1.tar.gz
	4. cd into R-2.11.1
	5. Unpack http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools/R64_Tcl_8-5-8.zip  ( see http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools )
	6. Unpack http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools/goodies/Win64/local64.zip  ( see http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/Rtools )
	7. cd src\gnuwin32
	8. copy MkRules.dist to MkRules.local
	9. modify settings in  MkRules.local such that:
		WIN = 64 
		LOCAL_SOFT = /the/path/where/local/unzipped/to/but/you/have/to/use/forward/slashes/even/though/this/is/Windows
	10. run "make all recommended"



Mark



	

	



